{
  "name": "Calendar list",
  "description": "Two calendars merged into one list, sorted by start with the all-day event first. Jinja cannot make a service call with `return_response`, so this source goes through the integration the way history does: one `op=list` request, one reply cached under the `l_` key hashed from the readable form `calendar|<ids>|<hours>`. The row count is deliberately not part of that key, so two lists over the same calendars are one fetch. `startsIn` and the printed clock time are both computed at resolve from the stored timestamp and the context clock, never stored, so a cached list stays right between fetches.",
